WEBVTT

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.200
What's wrong, Zora?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.340
You seem down.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.470
Leave me alone!

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.440
Are you worried about something?

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.120
Yusei, you're so nice.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.420
During the town meeting, they decided to 
replace my marionette clock with a new one.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.920
But isn't it broken?

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.620
Shut up!

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.900
That's sad.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.320
Yeah...

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.530
Why is she only nice to Yusei?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.430
Yusei reminds me of my son.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.980
He's smart, kind and attentive!

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.940
I know I'm not attentive!

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.290
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:28.830
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:33.410
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:39.070
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:44.110
There's no need to fear

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:51.750
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.890
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:03.530
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:09.120
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:17.040
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:49.310
Poppo Time's Old Clock

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.460
How's the balance now?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.960
Looking good!

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.240
Bruno, check mine next.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.840
How cool!

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.190
That D-Wheel's wings are awesome!

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.160
Right?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.130
And Wheel of Fortune is also cool!

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.580
Of course!

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.600
This D-Wheel is the only one in the world!

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.880
I also like dueling.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.310
But I haven't reached the 
level of having Riding Duels.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.580
Even I managed to get a license, 
so everyone has a chance.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.390
Anyway, who are you?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.720
I didn't know this place was 
converted into a D-Wheel garage!

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.320
Who is he?

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.690
Is he from a rival team in the WRGP?

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.120
This is our garage.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.390
Outsiders aren't allowed to enter!

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:44.700
You say I can't enter, but 
this used to be my room.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.430
Your room?  That means...

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.390
You finally understand!

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.270
That's right!

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.900
I'm Leo, Poppo Time's only son!

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.340
He's different from what we heard.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.950
You've already heard stories about me?

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.580
My mom must be bragging about me.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.820
I see.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.640
Every time Zora sees Crow, she's 
reminded of her no-good son.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.320
That's why she's mean to him.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.260
I understand.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:18.090
Maybe I shouldn't say this, but I'm 
that son she keeps bragging about!

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.810
I heard that you left 
three years ago to study.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.270
That's right!  I finished 
my training and came home!

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.900
It was three years ago.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.240
The marionette clock in front 
of the shop suddenly broke.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:37.500
I never studied clocks, 
but I'm a natural learner.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.920
I thought I'd know more than an amateur.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.280
However...

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.710
I had to give up.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:51.060
You can't fix it because you never tried to 
learn from your father while he was still alive!

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.560
He died before I could learn from him!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.530
No one knew he would die so early!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.000
Leo, how can you say that?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.460
And I ran out.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.410
You ran away.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.610
You're no good.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.650
You're the worst.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.180
If you put it that way...

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.380
But you trained because you 
thought you were no good, right?

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.150
Yeah, I trained a lot!

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.300
I'm now a semi-famous clock mechanic!

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:24.860
Pros always recommend me, and my 
master wants me to succeed him!

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.830
Then go meet Zora.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.830
Tell her you trained in 
order to fix the clock.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.800
Well...

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.840
You're worried that if you 
meet Zora, you'll fight again.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.300
That's right.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.910
Really?

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.020
Yeah.  The stronger the bond 
between a parent and a child,

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.610
the harder it is to find the right words.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.020
You're so right, lady!

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.120
If you want to fix the 
clock, you should hurry.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.890
During the town meeting, they decided 
to replace it with a new clock.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.460
Are you serious?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.600
Oh no!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.430
Wait!

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:01.790
Are you going dressed like that?

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.960
You should fix your appearance first.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.010
You're right.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.270
I don't know how to tie this.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.530
I'll do it!

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.400
{missing? if not, adjust timing accordingly}

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.630
Are you trying to kill him, Jack?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.240
For a necktie...

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:18.940
There.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.730
Well done.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.660
I sometimes tie my father's necktie.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:25.880
All good.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.790
All right!  Go, Leo!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.990
Go home for the first time in three years!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.770
Okay.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:38.700
Do your best, Leo!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.430
Welcome-

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.300
Leo!

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.550
I came home because I want 
to fix the clock in front.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.740
The clock?

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.700
It's still broken, right?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:57.130
I trained to become a clock mechanic.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.020
Clock?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.290
And I was pretty good at it!

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.820
I have natural talent!

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:08.350
My master said I'm a genius clock mechanic 
that only appears once every ten years!

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:12.500
So I'm just dropping by 
to fix the clock for you!

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.470
Does he think that's an apology?

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:19.900
"Dropping by to fix it?"

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:23.070
Who do you think broke that clock?

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.290
You broke it!

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.040
What's going on, Leo?

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.840
Well...

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.650
Three Years Ago

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.520
Winding this everyday is annoying.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.420
Who winds things these days?

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.590
We should switch to batteries!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.290
Huh?  This gear isn't moving.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.310
Oh, it's not connected.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.360
That means...

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.520
Connect it.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.520
Good.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.270
Huh?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.240
That one too?

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:58.250
Now over here?

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.580
And over here.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.270
And here!  And here!

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.950
What's going on?

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:15.360
You're confident that you can fix that clock?

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.280
Answer me!

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.440
I won't know until I try.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.840
That's what I thought!  Leave!

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.870
Forget you!

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.750
I'm closing the store for today!

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.640
Fine!

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.860
I'm never coming back!

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:31.840
Wait, Leo!

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:32.740
Hey!

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.630
You want to leave things like this?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:38.000
It's your chance to show the 
results of your training!

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.290
I don't want to!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.880
I didn't train for that stubborn woman!

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.050
Then why did you train?

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:46.220
Shut up!

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:49.560
You'll never understand because 
you're not her real son!

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:52.620
Fine.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.030
Then duel me before you leave!

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:58.000
A duel?

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.000
Yeah.  If you win, you 
can go wherever you like!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.640
But if I win, you have to apologize to Zora!

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.340
Zora is like a mother to us!

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:13.210
I won't let you get away 
with hurting our mother!

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.180
Fine.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.180
I accept the duel.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:19.650
I accept!

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.770
He's trying to force him 
to talk to Zora again.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:26.590
No.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.280
Since it's Crow, he's planning something.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.100
Duel!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.640
I summon Monster Clock!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.880
What?  0 attack points?

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.310
You're mocking me!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.850
I end my turn.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.450
My turn!

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:53.320
I summon Blackwing - Fane the Steel Chain!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.660
Crow, pummel him!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.300
Mom...

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:01.860
Hey!

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:05.870
Have you ever seriously confronted Zora?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.270
I confronted her!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.700
She's the one who doesn't want to listen!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.170
Really?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.970
I think that you don't have the guts.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:17.510
Whatever.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:21.400
By the time this duel is 
over, I'll know the answer.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:27.480
When a Blackwing is on my field, I can 
Special Summon this card from my hand!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.880
I Special Summon Gale the Whirlwind!

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.720
Go, Gale the Whirlwind!

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.880
Now's my chance!  I activate 
Monster Clock's effect!

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.130
Monster Clock swallows the attacking monster!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.100
What?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.350
Isn't it fun?

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:54.970
Monster Clock gains attack points 
equal to the monster it swallowed!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:59.920
Now Monster Clock has more 
attack points than Fane!

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.290
Be quiet!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:04.990
I can still attack you directly!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.620
Fane the Steel Chain, strike him!

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.430
I end my turn!

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.050
How dare you!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.590
It's my turn!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.960
I draw!

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.830
I summon Clock Knight No. 12 from my hand!

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:51.800
Then I activate the spell 
card Clockwork from my hand!

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:58.350
I can Special Summon a monster from my hand 
that has a lower Level than my Clock Knight!

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:02.240
I call forth Clock Knight No. 3!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:07.020
Clock Knight tosses a coin once per turn.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:12.820
If it's heads, it gains 1200 attack 
points until the End Phase.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.290
1200?

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:22.460
And if there's another Clock Knight on the 
field, I can negate the coin toss once and redo it.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:23.660
What?

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.170
He may be unexpectedly tough.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:30.170
He has Clock Knight No. 
3 and 12 on his field.

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:35.640
Since each lets him redo his coin toss, his 
effect has a greater chance of activating.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.700
I'll start with No. 12!

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:40.350
Heads is the sun!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.650
Come out, sun!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.620
It's the moon!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:52.090
Damn!  Due to Clock Knight No. 3's 
effect, I'll redo the coin toss!

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.780
Come out, sun!

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.900
There it is!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:03.130
Clock Knight No. 12 gains 1200 attack points!

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:10.180
Then due to Clock Knight No. 3's 
effect, I'll do another coin toss!

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.750
Sun!

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.350
Ta daa!

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.770
It's the sun!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.320
It also gains 1200 points!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.340
Battle!

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:27.500
Clock Knight No. 12 attacks 
Fane the Steel Chain!

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.700
I'm not done!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.390
No. 3 can still attack!

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:37.000
Clock Knight No. 3!

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.240
Attack him directly!

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:40.640
Not good enough!

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:45.240
I Special Summon Blackwing – Ghibli the 
Searing Wind from my hand in defense position!

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:49.950
I can Special Summon it from my 
hand when I'm directly attacked!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.380
Stop the attack!

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.050
Clock Knight No. 3 doesn't have 
enough attack points to defeat it.

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:57.790
I stop the attack.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:59.360
I end my turn.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.830
You redo your effects even 
though it's a gambling deck?

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.460
Stop using weak strategies!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:09.070
There are no redos in life!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.730
It's my turn!

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.500
Mirror Force destroys all 
monsters in attack position.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:15.300
All right!

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.510
I set this card!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.610
Here I go!

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.960
I summon Blackwing – 
Blizzard the Far North!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.480
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.820
I can Special Summon Fane the Steel Chain 
from my graveyard in defense position!

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:34.020
Here I go!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:38.040
Level 2 Blizzard the Far North 
tunes Level 2 Fane the Steel Chain

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.060
and Level 3 Ghibli the Searing Wind!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.700
Black wind, turn into wings 
that rise to the heavens!

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.980
Synchro Summon!

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.860
Blackwing Armor Master!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:54.340
Battle!

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:58.080
Armor Master attacks Clock Knight No. 3!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.550
Destroy!  Black Hurricane!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.000
I quit.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:18.700
You're quitting?

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:25.580
What can I do when you have a monster with 2500 
attack points that can't be destroyed in battle?

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:26.670
Stop acting spoiled!

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.640
You're going to give up without trying?

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.880
You're all talk!  When you're in trouble, 
you only think about running away!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.080
Why won't you face Zora?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.040
You trained, right?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.190
Don't you have the confidence to fix it?

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.160
Shut up!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.790
This is sloppy work!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.930
Can't you take care of your tools?

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:54.870
Damn.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.010
Damn!

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.610
You don't have the confidence 
to fix the clock.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.940
Nor to confront Zora.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.080
Nor the confidence to confront 
your father's clock!

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.050
You don't care about anything!

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:16.220
Zora was fed up because you 
came home with that attitude!

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:17.990
I end my turn!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.920
Try to act more seriously!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.450
My turn.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:24.600
I draw.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:29.590
This belonged to my father.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.310
What's wrong?

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.770
Did mom scold you again?

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:37.610
Yeah.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:40.780
For my essay, I wrote that I wanted 
to be a duelist when I grow up.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:44.400
She was mad that I didn't 
want to be a watchmaker!

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.290
I see.  You're in a difficult position.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:51.450
But mom scolds you because 
she cares about you.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:54.530
Here.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.150
It's Time Wizard!

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.830
It's a very rare card!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.530
You wanted it, right?

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:01.260
Yeah!

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.600
Thank you!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.970
You should choose the path you want to take.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:12.250
If there's something you want to 
do, then do it with all your might.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:15.960
That's right.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:19.580
I'm going to use this card!

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.920
I summon Time Wizard!

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.560
Time Wizard?

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.820
My father gave me this card!

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:31.030
I believe in this card!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:33.100
I activate Time Roulette!

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.810
If the roulette is successful, 
all your monsters are destroyed!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.450
If it fails, all my monsters are destroyed!

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:44.540
And I take damage equal to half the total 
attack points of my destroyed monsters!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:49.780
Even though Armor Master is invincible in 
battle, Time Wizard's effect can destroy it.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:52.590
Spin, roulette of destiny!

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.750
Guide me to victory!

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:01.660
What's this?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.760
Is Time Wizard showing this to me?

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.630
What's up?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.040
Do you enjoy watching?

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:09.800
Yeah!

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.040
That's right.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:15.180
I loved to watch my father repair watches.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:15.770
Father.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.520
Father.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:21.320
Mom scolds you because she cares about you.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:22.970
Mom...

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:29.320
Time Roulette, be successful!

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:35.890
It's successful!

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:38.990
Time Wizard destroys Armor Master!

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.460
Time Magic!

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.900
Battle!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:55.070
Monster Clock and Clock Knight 
No. 12 attack you directly!

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.910
If this attack succeeds, Crow loses.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:02.750
But he would've anticipated this situation.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.650
That set card is the key 
to turning the tables!

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.200
Crow...

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.710
...lost.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.800
You win.

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.350
No one will stop you.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.910
Hurry up and leave this city!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.380
You want to leave, right?

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.550
You won.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:40.590
Do whatever you like!

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.290
I'm not leaving!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.320
You were right!

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:57.420
My master yelled at me everyday until 
he finally let me work on clocks.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:00.940
The more I learned about clocks, the more 
I realized how incredible my father was!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.340
My father's marionette 
clock is a masterpiece!

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:11.210
After training, I now know that 
I couldn't have easily fixed it!

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:15.390
I regret that my father died 
before I learned about his job!

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.590
That I broke my father's masterpiece!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:22.290
That I couldn't live up 
to my mom's expectations!

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.490
My father's clock is here!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.960
My mom is here!

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:29.170
This place is irreplaceable to me!

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:31.370
So where am I supposed to go?

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:33.840
Leo...

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.140
I'll fix that clock!

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:40.980
Leo...

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:45.010
Crow, you lost on purpose to 
uncover Leo's true feelings.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.360
How clever.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.490
Thank you.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:56.300
He gets his stubbornness from his mother.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:05.850
It works!

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.780
Everyone!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.940
Wow!  It's working!

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:18.910
The clock is fixed!

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.140
He did it!

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:22.380
Mom.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:24.590
Mom!

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:25.950
Leo...

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.390
Leo!

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:28.780
Mom!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:31.090
Well done!

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:32.560
Mom!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.240
You're like your father!

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:37.070
You're my son!

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:40.750
Mom!

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:14.690
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:19.570
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:24.510
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:29.520
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:34.570
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:41.130
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:45.200
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:51.040
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:55.130
Bond is the proper word

00:22:55.130 --> 00:23:00.750
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:03.930
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:06.190
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:10.720
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.690
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:17.130
You want to party until the morning

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:20.510
At our special place
